# Binary fixtures must survive checkout byte for byte.
#
# Without this, git's line-ending conversion can rewrite LF to CRLF on Windows. That corrupts
# any file whose format counts bytes. A PDF stores byte offsets in its xref table, so a
# converted checkout yields "this PDF has no pages" on one platform only, pointing nowhere
# near the cause.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff2 binary
